+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"feat-001","node_id":"N1","attempt":2,"source":"david","source_ref":"loop.jsonl steer(D1,pause2): reviewer A2 findings R1, R4, R5 (docs/trace/feat-001/N1/verdicts/A2-reviewer.json)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"LRN-5","layer":"tests","files":["docs/guides/api/index.html","docs/guides/api/run-receipts.sh","docs/guides/api/receipts.md"],"root_cause":"Symptom (R1): from 2026-10-26 onwards, a reader following the servicer journey gets 422 SELL-2 on the GUIDE-002 sale, and the later GUIDE-002 steps then fail too. Cause: every request in the journey uses a fixed date that only works on the capture day, and the guide never tells the reader to move them. The commands are recorded as fixed strings in run-receipts.sh:90-109: C01 starts 2026-11-01, C03 and C05 use 2026-11-10, C08 starts 2026-10-25, F08 uses 2026-10-24, C09 uses 2026-10-25 and F06 uses 2026-10-26. The script comment at run-receipts.sh:5-6 admits 'the dates in the commands below only fit that day'. The guide copies them as they are (index.html:806, :840, :982). The only explanation is the summary at index.html:760, which says 'today is 2026-10-25' but never tells the reader to move the dates to their own today. The only hint is the troubleshooting row at index.html:1234. This breaks LRN-5 ('the exact command ... and what you should see') and feat-001.dag.yaml:33 ('A reader follows one persona journey in a PDF against the running app and reaches each step's shown result'). SELL-2 accepts a start date only from today to today + 60 (index.html:103). So C08 fails from 2026-10-26, C01 fails after 2026-11-01, the CANCEL-3 and COULD-2a examples (F08, F06) stop showing what they are meant to show, and C09's claim date stops being today. A second effect: the outputs shown (daysUsed, refundAmount at index.html:919, :927, :979, quotedOn, and the SELL-2 window detail at :828) are tied to 2026-10-25. Even dates moved correctly reproduce them only if every date moves by the same offset, and the guide doesn't say which values will then differ. The symptom is the 422 on a later day; the cause is fixed capture-day dates with no instruction to move them. Fix direction: make each servicer-journey date relative to the reader's own today, either by a clear instruction with the offsets from today or by dates the reader's shell works out. Keep the commands receipted, since checks A1/I1 and A1/I4 in check.test.mjs:101-111 and :156-163 require the guide's command text to match a receipts.md Command line. Say plainly which shown values (dates, days and refund amounts, quotedOn) will differ from the reader's run and why. Carried from F7 A2 R4 and A2.2 R4 (other plans); this is the first fix attempt on this node.","fingerprint":"LRN-5|docs/guides/api/index.html|fixed-capture-day-dates","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given docs/guides/api/index.html's servicer journey (section#servicer), When node --test docs/guides/api/check.test.mjs scans every curl command in it for a fixed yyyy-MM-dd value in a request body or query, Then each such date is either worked out from the reader's today or covered by an explicit instruction in that section to move it by a stated offset, and the test fails on the guide as at a9c3f83b, where C08's startDate 2026-10-25 (index.html:840) has neither (docs/guides/api/check.test.mjs, a new LRN-5 check)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"LRN-5","layer":"tests","files":["docs/guides/api/index.html","docs/guides/api/run-receipts.sh"],"root_cause":"Symptom (R4): on a clean machine, DJ3's `dotnet ef migrations script ...` (index.html:211) isn't found. Cause: the guide never makes dotnet-ef a prerequisite, and the repository has nothing that would supply it. DJ2 step 1 (index.html:125-128) lists only the .NET SDK. There is no .config/dotnet-tools.json (no tool manifest in the worktree), so the `dotnet tool restore` the guide quotes from pre-push (index.html:612) restores nothing, as receipts.md:716-718 records. The R8 output shown at index.html:213-215 ('tools version 9.0.9 is older than ... 10.0.13') proves the capture used a global tool already on that machine; run-receipts.sh:132 runs `dotnet ef` without installing it. dotnet-ef appears only in the troubleshooting row at index.html:1238, which is about an older version, not a missing one. This breaks LRN-5's 'the exact command or click' for each step, and §6 'migrations' as numbered steps with real output. The symptom is 'command not found'; the cause is a missing prerequisite step. Fix direction: add the dotnet-ef install, at the runtime's EF version, as a numbered prerequisite before DJ3. Run it through run-receipts.sh so it gets a receipt (check A1/I4, check.test.mjs:156-163, fails on any command shown without one). Make the troubleshooting row at :1238 agree with it. Adding a repository tool manifest instead would change how pre-push behaves, which is outside a docs node; that is David's call, not the builder's.","fingerprint":"LRN-5|docs/guides/api/index.html|dotnet-ef-prerequisite-missing","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given docs/guides/api/index.html, When node --test docs/guides/api/check.test.mjs finds the first command starting `dotnet ef`, Then an earlier step in the guide shows a receipted command that installs or restores dotnet-ef, and the test fails on the guide as at a9c3f83b, where DJ3 (index.html:211) has none before it (docs/guides/api/check.test.mjs, a new LRN-5 check)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I3","rule_id":"§8.3","layer":"tests","files":["docs/guides/api/run-receipts.sh","docs/guides/api/receipts.md"],"root_cause":"Symptom (R5): receipts.md:719 says 'At HEAD, one architecture test fails', but gate.test at 0e0cc637 passed 652/652 (packet/gates.jsonl:6), and the node's HEAD is a9c3f83b. Cause: the note is fixed text that dates itself only by the moving word 'HEAD'. It is written in a quoted heredoc in run-receipts.sh:146-159 (the bullet at :155), so it never reflects the commit it describes. The receipts were captured at 6bf608d2 (every entry's 'Date: ... at 6bf608d2' line, receipts.md:14 and following). There the note was true. The later commit da7ac832 then fixed docs/guides/ui/run-output.json:45 without changing the note in either the script or receipts.md. So 'At HEAD' now describes a HEAD where the failure no longer exists, and it contradicts the file's own R3 and R3d results, which show 'failed: 0' (receipts.md:51, :115). This breaks §8 acceptance 3 (documentation-requirements.md:195-197): receipts are the evidence, and nothing in them may be wrong. The symptom is the wrong sentence in receipts.md; the cause is in run-receipts.sh:155, because receipts.md is generated from it and a rerun would bring the stale wording back. Fix direction: in the script and in receipts.md alike, tie the note to the capture commit it was true at (6bf608d2) instead of 'HEAD', and say the failure was fixed by da7ac832. Or rerun the receipts at the current commit and drop or rewrite the note to match. Either way the 'run as committed' counts must still describe the commit they were measured on.","fingerprint":"§8.3|docs/guides/api/run-receipts.sh|stale-at-head-note","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given docs/guides/api/receipts.md, When node --test docs/guides/api/check.test.mjs reads the 'Observed while capturing' section, Then no bullet says 'At HEAD' (any statement of a test result names the commit it was measured at, matching the entries' 'at <sha>' lines), and the test fails on receipts.md:719 and run-receipts.sh:155 as at a9c3f83b (docs/guides/api/check.test.mjs, a new §8.3 check)","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["A1: gate.write failed at 6f2e8efc because check A1/I8 counted 7 diagram rows, not the 30 questions (fingerprint none|docs/guides/api/check.test.mjs|stale-question-id-pattern); fixed in 1f548620","A2: reviewer PASS with 7 P2s and security PASS at a9c3f83b; no fix tried yet for R1, R4 or R5, and none of their causes repeats the A1 fingerprint"]}
